module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GeneratedIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.RingIdealSite

/-!
# The complex `K^•_{U, I}` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] as a complex of presheaves of modules

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪` — on a slice site
`𝒞/U` this is the data of finitely many sections of `𝒪` over `U`, and `I = (f_1, …, f_r)` is the
finitely generated ideal of `𝒪(U)` they span. The proof of [Stacks, Tag 099E] attaches to it the
complex of presheaves

`K^•_{U, I} : U'/U ⟼ K(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))`

with `K(-, -)` the complex of [Stacks, Tag 099D]. This file builds it, as a genuine complex of
presheaves of `𝒪`-modules together with its augmentation onto the structure presheaf.

The construction has two steps, and the point of both is that no choice is made twice. First,
the assignment `U' ↦ (𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))` is a functor
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor` to the category
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal` of rings with an ideal: the ideal spanned by the values of the
`f_i` over `U'` is generated by the image of the ideal spanned over `U`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan_map_eq`, exactly the condition a morphism of rings with
an ideal asks for. Second, `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` is a complex of presheaves of
modules on rings with an ideal, so pulling it back along that functor gives the complex on `𝒞`.

Nothing of the Čech construction is redone: `K(A, I)` is the filtered colimit of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenSetCechColimit.lean`, whose value depends on the pair `(A, I)`
alone.

## Independence of the generators

[Stacks, Tag 099E] compares the complexes obtained from two finitely generated ideals `I` and
`I'` of `𝒪(U)` which generate the same sheaf of ideals `ℐ|_U`. The two objectwise ideals need not
agree, but they agree above a covering sieve of `U` —
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq` — and *there the two functors to rings
with an ideal are literally equal*, hence so are the two pullbacks. That is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor_comp_eq` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.rightOp_comp_eq`, which is the form in which
sheafification-locality for a covering sieve consumes the comparison: equal restrictions, not
merely isomorphic ones.

On the category `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair r` of rings carrying a *chosen family of `r`
elements*, two ideals with different numbers of generators give presheaves on two different
categories `GenPair r` and `GenPair s`, between which there is nothing to compare. Forgetting the
chosen family — which the value of `K` never uses — is what makes the comparison possible.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor`: the functor `𝒞ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingIdeal` attached to a
  finite family of global sections of `𝒪`, sending an object to its ring of sections together
  with the ideal the family spans there.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionIdealPullback`: the pullback of presheaves of modules
  along it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionIdealCechComplex`: **the complex `K^•_{U, I}`**, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionIdealCechAugmentation` its augmentation onto the structure
  presheaf.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan_map_eq`: **the objectwise ideal of a restriction is
  generated by the image of the objectwise ideal**, which is what makes the assignment
  functorial.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionIdealCechComplex_obj`: the value of the complex at an
  object is the complex `K(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))` of [Stacks, Tag 099D].
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor_comp_eq` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.rightOp_comp_eq`: **two families spanning the same objectwise
  ideal above a subcategory give the same complex there**, degreewise and with the same
  augmentation.

## Implementation notes

The functor to rings with an ideal is contravariant on the site, so it is a functor `𝒞ᵒᵖ ⥤
RingIdeal`; `CategoryTheory.Functor.rightOp` turns it into the `𝒞 ⥤ RingIdealᵒᵖ` that
`PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀` consumes, the site of a presheaf of modules on rings with an
ideal being `RingIdealᵒᵖ`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. [Stacks, Tag 099E] asserts the existence of a *global* map
`K → 𝒪` of `D(𝒪)` whose restriction to every object over which `ℐ` is finitely generated is the
extended alternating Čech complex; what is built here is the presheaf complex of its proof, on
one object and for one choice of generators.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w u₂ v₂

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

open Stacks.RingIdealSite

section Functor

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The objectwise ideal of a restriction is generated by the image of the objectwise ideal.**
The `f_i` are global sections, so restriction carries their values over `U` to their values over
`V`; the two ideals are spanned by the two families, and the image of a span is the span of the
image.

This is the sharpening of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.map_mem_sectionSpan` from an inclusion to
an equality, and it is exactly the condition that a morphism of
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal` requires. -/
theorem sectionSpan_map_eq {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V) :
    sectionSpan f V = Ideal.map (X.O.obj.map g).hom (sectionSpan f U) := by
  rw [sectionSpan, sectionSpan, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  exact congrArg (fun h : Fin r → X.O.obj.obj V ↦ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
    (funext fun i ↦ (globalSectionVal_map (f i) g).symm)

/-- **The functor to rings with an ideal attached to a finite family of global sections of
`𝒪`**: an object `U` of the site goes to its ring of sections together with the ideal
`(f_1|_U, …, f_r|_U)` spanned there, and a morphism to the restriction map, which carries the
ideal onto the ideal by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sectionSpan_map_eq`.

Pulling `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` back along this functor is the complex `K^•_{U, I}`
of [Stacks, Tag 099E]. -/
def ringIdealFunctor : X.Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingIdeal.{w} :=
  ofIdealAssignment X.O.obj (sectionSpan f) fun {_ _} g ↦ sectionSpan_map_eq f g

/-- The ring of `ringIdealFunctor f` at `U` is the ring of sections `𝒪(U)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringIdealFunctor_obj_ring (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((ringIdealFunctor f).obj U).ring = X.O.obj.obj U := rfl

/-- The ideal of `ringIdealFunctor f` at `U` is the ideal of `𝒪(U)` spanned by the `f_i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringIdealFunctor_obj_ideal (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((ringIdealFunctor f).obj U).ideal = sectionSpan f U := rfl

/-- The ring homomorphism underlying `ringIdealFunctor f` on a morphism `g` is the restriction
map of `𝒪` along `g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringIdealFunctor_map_toRingHom {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V) :
    ((ringIdealFunctor f).map g).toRingHom = (X.O.obj.map g).hom := rfl

end Functor

section Complex

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))

/-- **The pullback of presheaves of modules along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor`.** A presheaf of modules on the category of rings
with an ideal becomes a presheaf of `𝒪`-modules on the site. -/
abbrev sectionIdealPullback :
    RingIdealModule.{w} ⥤
      PresheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj :=
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (ringIdealFunctor f).rightOp structureRings.{w}

/-- Restriction of presheaves of modules along a functor preserves zero morphisms: a morphism is
carried to the morphism with the same components, and the zero morphism has zero components. -/
instance preservesZeroMorphisms_sectionIdealPullback :
    (sectionIdealPullback f).PreservesZeroMorphisms where
  map_zero _ _ := PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- **The complex `K^•_{U, I}` of [Stacks, Tag 099E]**, as a complex of presheaves of
`𝒪`-modules: the pullback along `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor` of the complex
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` of [Stacks, Tag 099D]. Its value at an object `U` is
`K(𝒪(U), I𝒪(U))`. -/
abbrev sectionIdealCechComplex :
    CochainComplex (PresheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj) ℕ :=
  (((sectionIdealPullback f).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ))).obj kComplexNat.{w}

/-- The term of `sectionIdealCechComplex f` in degree `n` is the pullback of the degree-`n` term
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.kTerm n`. -/
theorem sectionIdealCechComplex_X (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionIdealCechComplex f).X n = (sectionIdealPullback f).obj (kTerm.{w} n) := rfl

/-- The value of the degree-`n` term of `sectionIdealCechComplex f` at `U` is the colimit of the
Čech term diagram of the ring `𝒪(U)` and the ideal spanned there by the `f_i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sectionIdealCechComplex_obj (n : ℕ) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((sectionIdealCechComplex f).X n).obj U =
      (colimit (Stacks.GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.O.obj.obj U) (sectionSpan f U) n) :
        ModuleCat.{w} (X.O.obj.obj U)) := rfl

/-- **The augmentation of `K^•_{U, I}` onto the structure presheaf**, the pullback of
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.kAugZero`. -/
abbrev sectionIdealCechAugmentation :
    (sectionIdealCechComplex f).X 0 ⟶
      PresheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj :=
  (sectionIdealPullback f).map kAugZero.{w}

end Complex

section Agreement

variable {X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}} {r s : ℕ}
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
  (g : Fin s → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{w}))
  {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] (ι : D ⥤ X.C)

/-- **Two finite families of global sections spanning the same objectwise ideal at every object
of a subcategory give the same functor to rings with an ideal there**, hence the same complex
`K^•` there, degreewise and with the same augmentation.

This is the step of [Stacks, Tag 099E] which says that the complex `K^•_{U, I}` depends on the
chosen finitely generated ideal `I ⊆ ℐ(U)` only through the objectwise ideals it spans: above the
covering sieve of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq` those agree, so the
restrictions of the two complexes to it are *equal*, not merely isomorphic, which is what
sheafification-locality for a covering sieve consumes. -/
theorem ringIdealFunctor_comp_eq
    (h : ∀ d : Dᵒᵖ, sectionSpan f (op (ι.obj d.unop)) = sectionSpan g (op (ι.obj d.unop))) :
    ι.op ⋙ ringIdealFunctor f = ι.op ⋙ ringIdealFunctor g :=
  comp_ofIdealAssignment_eq X.O.obj ι _ _ h

/-- **Two finite families of global sections spanning the same objectwise ideal at every object
of a subcategory give the same pullback datum there**: the two functors `D ⥤ RingIdealᵒᵖ` which
`PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀` consumes coincide. -/
theorem rightOp_comp_eq
    (h : ∀ d : Dᵒᵖ, sectionSpan f (op (ι.obj d.unop)) = sectionSpan g (op (ι.obj d.unop))) :
    ι ⋙ (ringIdealFunctor f).rightOp = ι ⋙ (ringIdealFunctor g).rightOp :=
  congrArg CategoryTheory.Functor.rightOp (ringIdealFunctor_comp_eq f g ι h)

end Agreement

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
